\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Reynolds-number dependence of the full model (ensemble means, $N=100$ per $\nu $, $\pm \sigma $; centroid curves lightly smoothed), for $\nu =10^{-4},\,5\times 10^{-5},\,2\times 10^{-5},\,1.42\times 10^{-5},\,10^{-5}, \,10^{-6},\,10^{-7}$. (\textit  {a}) Final-strain spectrum $E(k)=\DOTSI \sumop \slimits@ _i E_i(k)$; the cascade extends further toward high $k$ as $\nu $ falls. The dotted line marks a $k^{-5/3}$ slope for reference. At the two smallest $\nu $ the spectrum flattens into a grid-scale shelf at the cutoff (under-resolved). (\textit  {b}) Centroid migration per $\nu $ against the linear-RDT line (dashed). The resolved cases ($\nu \gtrsim 10^{-5}$) lie below the line; the two lowest-$\nu $ cases exceed it but carry the widest $\sigma $ bands, reflecting the under-resolved grid-scale energy in (\textit  {a}).}}{23}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
